       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is about 5 times the maximum daily dose for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single dose is usually 400\u2013800 mg, and the over-the-counter limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg** PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
