       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, is 16,000 mg/day. No indication supports that, and it's in the range where serious toxicity is expected. If it were entered, it could reach the patient before anyone caught it.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If it was a typo or unit mix-up**, give me the intended dose. For example, 400 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- **If you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect**, ibuprofen is capped at 3,200 mg/day. I can enter a maximum-dose ibuprofen order, or you could add or switch to another agent such as scheduled acetaminophen, with your choice of drug and dose.\n- **If you believe this dose is intended**, please talk to pharmacy or a clinical pharmacologist first. The order would need to go through your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
